1
00:00:09,320 --> 00:00:12,960
Brighten it up and try
stepping away for a while.

2
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:28,460
Like someone calling out to you,
after the rain.

3
00:00:29,880 --> 00:00:35,320
Walking while looking back,
led along by the hand of Gā-chan.

4
00:00:36,180 --> 00:00:42,460
That mysterious feeling I had back then.

5
00:00:43,180 --> 00:00:47,740
So on the arcade street's tiles,

6
00:00:47,740 --> 00:00:53,520
I tried walking only on the black ones.

7
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:59,680
Everyone was a child once,

8
00:00:59,680 --> 00:01:01,820
but everyone has forgotten.

9
00:01:02,760 --> 00:01:09,120
Politicians with their self-important faces,
and that aunt who's a thorn in your side, too.

10
00:01:09,640 --> 00:01:14,700
Try turning at that corner over there.

11
00:01:15,740 --> 00:01:19,900
You can meet everyone, everyone.

12
00:01:22,140 --> 00:01:27,840
Over there is Kame-ari.
Well, surely there's a turtle, Kame-ari.

13
00:01:29,340 --> 00:01:33,040
Everyone, come on over to our town!

14
00:01:34,160 --> 00:01:34,600
Thank you.

15
00:01:37,240 --> 00:01:39,500
Let's head home fueled by calcium!

16
00:01:45,780 --> 00:01:47,300
The jig is up.

17
00:01:47,300 --> 00:01:49,180
Why don't you just confess already?

18
00:01:50,480 --> 00:01:53,400
Your eyebrows are connected, you know.

19
00:01:53,400 --> 00:01:56,740
Don't mess with me!
Are you going to confess or not?

20
00:01:57,840 --> 00:01:59,040
I'll spill, I'll spill.

21
00:01:59,040 --> 00:01:59,520
Really?

22
00:01:59,760 --> 00:02:01,860
If it's a settlement of around a million yen,
then sure.

23
00:02:02,820 --> 00:02:03,720
You bastard!

24
00:02:04,140 --> 00:02:06,120
Stop spouting that crap!

25
00:02:06,120 --> 00:02:07,620
Are you going to spill it or not!

26
00:02:09,320 --> 00:02:11,500
Stop the violence! Call my lawyer!

27
00:02:11,760 --> 00:02:13,820
Call whoever you want, just settle it!

28
00:02:13,860 --> 00:02:15,200
Stop it!

29
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:18,520
Not yet!

30
00:02:18,720 --> 00:02:21,160
If you don't want to meet your maker,
spill it already!

31
00:02:21,560 --> 00:02:24,180
You go first, please!

32
00:02:25,240 --> 00:02:26,320
If you can't talk!

33
00:02:26,400 --> 00:02:26,840
Honda!

34
00:02:27,840 --> 00:02:30,900
We just rough this crook up
and squeeze it out of him!

35
00:02:31,280 --> 00:02:33,340
He's not a real crook!

36
00:02:34,840 --> 00:02:37,540
That's right!
This is an interrogation contest!

37
00:02:38,220 --> 00:02:39,800
H-hey, pull yourself together!

38
00:02:39,980 --> 00:02:41,720
Oh no! Take it from the top!

39
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:45,340
Is this how you always conduct
interrogations at your station?

40
00:02:46,060 --> 00:02:48,060
N-no, never like that...

41
00:02:48,060 --> 00:02:50,400
This was where I was just getting started!

42
00:02:50,920 --> 00:02:54,200
Another little beating
and he would have confessed!

43
00:02:55,780 --> 00:02:57,260
That's a problematic statement, isn't it.

44
00:02:57,260 --> 00:02:59,320
It damages the police's image.

45
00:02:59,320 --> 00:02:59,720
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

46
00:02:59,720 --> 00:03:04,920
Wait, I haven't finished scoring yet!

47
00:03:04,920 --> 00:03:05,620
Scoring?

48
00:03:05,900 --> 00:03:09,720
I only joined because you said
the bonus would double if I won.

49
00:03:10,240 --> 00:03:11,740
No need to score it.

50
00:03:11,740 --> 00:03:14,780
How would you know without scoring it?

51
00:03:14,780 --> 00:03:16,500
Then I'll score it for you.

52
00:03:16,500 --> 00:03:17,060
Yes!

53
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:23,320
X? No, Roman numerals.

54
00:03:24,200 --> 00:03:26,160
That means you're
disqualified with one strike!

55
00:03:26,280 --> 00:03:28,600
Then what about my bonus?

56
00:03:28,980 --> 00:03:31,360
As if you'd get one! No bonus!

57
00:03:32,300 --> 00:03:32,660
Damn it!

58
00:03:32,820 --> 00:03:34,540
No way!

59
00:03:35,500 --> 00:03:36,240
Damn it!

60
00:03:37,040 --> 00:03:40,980
I was trying to boost my bonus,
and now I'm losing it instead!

61
00:03:41,480 --> 00:03:44,740
Honestly, Ryo-chan,
your methods are way too rough.

62
00:03:45,060 --> 00:03:45,920
Why not!?

63
00:03:46,180 --> 00:03:48,520
In period dramas,
they do much worse than this!

64
00:03:49,880 --> 00:03:50,838
Unlike the old days,

65
00:03:50,888 --> 00:03:54,080
we have to consider human rights now,
you know.

66
00:03:54,480 --> 00:03:57,322
Interrogations require
perseverance and patience.

67
00:03:57,372 --> 00:03:59,000
Like Chief Ohara.

68
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:02,840
What's the Chief got that I don't?
I've got perseverance and patience too!

69
00:04:03,100 --> 00:04:05,266
I've built a hundred tank models,

70
00:04:05,316 --> 00:04:07,680
and played video games for
forty-eight hours straight!

71
00:04:08,180 --> 00:04:09,780
Sorry, the ball...

72
00:04:10,240 --> 00:04:13,340
So it was you...
who just hit me with the ball...

73
00:04:13,340 --> 00:04:14,800
S-sorry...

74
00:04:14,800 --> 00:04:16,820
Don't you dare play around here again!

75
00:04:21,100 --> 00:04:24,560
Where was your perseverance and
patience in that attitude just now?

76
00:04:25,060 --> 00:04:27,540
That was just a light joke, right!

77
00:04:29,680 --> 00:04:33,700
I came all this way to bring you news about restoring your bonus,
but...

78
00:04:33,700 --> 00:04:35,440
My bonus is back?

79
00:04:35,600 --> 00:04:37,980
Judging by your attitude just now,
that was wasted effort.

80
00:04:37,980 --> 00:04:41,060
Then you should have said so sooner, Chief!

81
00:04:42,040 --> 00:04:43,640
You're a disgusting one, aren't you.

82
00:04:43,640 --> 00:04:45,060
Well, never mind. Follow me.

83
00:04:45,060 --> 00:04:46,640
Yes sir, I'll follow you anywhere!

84
00:04:48,720 --> 00:04:50,120
Debate school?

85
00:04:50,520 --> 00:04:51,580
Come on, let's go.

86
00:04:51,580 --> 00:04:51,920
Yes.

87
00:04:53,140 --> 00:04:54,460
We've been waiting for you.

88
00:04:54,980 --> 00:04:56,900
I'm the principal of this school.

89
00:04:57,400 --> 00:04:58,900
It's a debate you're bound to win.

90
00:04:59,700 --> 00:05:01,200
I'm Ohara from Katsushika Station.

91
00:05:01,200 --> 00:05:04,120
And this is the notorious Kankichi Ryotsu.

92
00:05:04,120 --> 00:05:06,660
Please stop it, Chief.

93
00:05:06,660 --> 00:05:08,740
What kind of school is this, anyway?

94
00:05:09,360 --> 00:05:10,800
I told you, it's a debate.

95
00:05:10,800 --> 00:05:13,120
Debate... isn't that a bribe?

96
00:05:13,120 --> 00:05:15,400
You mean "rebate," don't you?

97
00:05:17,360 --> 00:05:20,160
Debate is a formal argument contest.

98
00:05:20,160 --> 00:05:24,240
For example, you pick a topic
like socialism versus democracy,

99
00:05:24,240 --> 00:05:27,620
argue over which is better, and try
to talk your opponent into submission.

100
00:05:28,160 --> 00:05:30,120
The audience decides who wins or loses.

101
00:05:31,420 --> 00:05:34,140
Well, you could say it's
a sport played with words.

102
00:05:35,300 --> 00:05:37,360
What, so basically it's just a verbal fight?

103
00:05:37,360 --> 00:05:39,360
It's not just a verbal fight.

104
00:05:39,760 --> 00:05:43,200
You have to convince everyone
around you using words alone.

105
00:05:43,200 --> 00:05:44,560
Perseverance and patience.

106
00:05:44,560 --> 00:05:49,320
On top of that, you need very
advanced rhetorical techniques.

107
00:05:50,700 --> 00:05:54,760
Your biggest problem is that your
hands move before your mouth does.

108
00:05:54,760 --> 00:05:59,600
You'll attend this school for two
weeks and fix that temper of yours.

109
00:05:59,600 --> 00:06:04,620
Two weeks?! I have to put up with
this old geezer for two whole weeks?

110
00:06:05,020 --> 00:06:07,540
It's not "ossan," it's "debate."

111
00:06:07,540 --> 00:06:10,080
Otherwise, there's no bonus for you.

112
00:06:10,080 --> 00:06:11,580
Fine, fine.

113
00:06:12,680 --> 00:06:13,480
Anyway,

114
00:06:14,360 --> 00:06:19,060
I've been wondering since earlier, why is the
"tsu" character so small?

115
00:06:20,600 --> 00:06:22,160
W-what's wrong, Sensei?

116
00:06:22,160 --> 00:06:27,540
You've already lost.

117
00:06:27,540 --> 00:06:28,940
W-what?

118
00:06:29,620 --> 00:06:31,080
Haven't you noticed yet?

119
00:06:31,080 --> 00:06:36,020
You've fallen perfectly
into the debate trap I set.

120
00:06:36,020 --> 00:06:38,280
A trap? What do you mean?

121
00:06:38,280 --> 00:06:41,600
Anyone would immediately notice that the small
"tsu" character is small.

122
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:44,900
It's the kind of thing that
makes you want to ask a question.

123
00:06:46,240 --> 00:06:50,140
But of course, the one being
questioned has anticipated that too.

124
00:06:50,140 --> 00:06:52,640
They should have a flawless
answer prepared as well.

125
00:06:52,640 --> 00:06:53,800
Therefore,

126
00:06:53,800 --> 00:06:57,760
once you carelessly touch on that topic,

127
00:06:57,760 --> 00:07:00,260
you're assailed by
rock-solid theoretical armor

128
00:07:02,120 --> 00:07:05,300
and battered until you're utterly broken.

129
00:07:06,080 --> 00:07:08,440
This is the Katta-ryū debate technique!

130
00:07:12,340 --> 00:07:14,660
First, I'll intimidate you with your name.

131
00:07:14,900 --> 00:07:17,120
A true debate pro.

132
00:07:17,120 --> 00:07:19,720
Something about this still seems fishy.

133
00:07:20,520 --> 00:07:23,760
I'm telling you, if you don't
get your diploma from the teacher,

134
00:07:23,760 --> 00:07:26,020
there's no bonus, got it?

135
00:07:26,020 --> 00:07:28,160
Yes, yes, I understand.

136
00:07:28,160 --> 00:07:30,100
So I just have to take the
classes seriously, right?

137
00:07:31,320 --> 00:07:33,340
What's important during an interrogation is

138
00:07:33,340 --> 00:07:35,560
first, to talk with the other person.

139
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:37,860
Any trivial topic will do,

140
00:07:38,240 --> 00:07:39,900
so first, start a conversation.

141
00:07:39,900 --> 00:07:42,000
No matter what the other person says,

142
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:44,000
you must never resort to violence.

143
00:07:45,280 --> 00:07:46,300
What is it, Ryotsu-kun?

144
00:07:46,940 --> 00:07:49,720
Why is the ツ in the teacher's
name written so small?

145
00:07:50,560 --> 00:07:52,680
I already told you that's a trap too.

146
00:07:52,680 --> 00:07:54,720
I can't help it, I'm curious.

147
00:07:54,720 --> 00:07:57,500
A rock-solid arsenal of
arguments is waiting for you.

148
00:07:57,500 --> 00:07:59,740
That's the arsenal I want to hear about.

149
00:08:05,080 --> 00:08:08,140
Now, the other important point is

150
00:08:08,140 --> 00:08:09,520
Hey, don't dodge the question.

151
00:08:09,520 --> 00:08:11,320
Keep talking persistently.

152
00:08:11,320 --> 00:08:14,820
Hey! You haven't actually prepared any arguments,
have you?

153
00:08:15,700 --> 00:08:19,640
Aren't you just acting so tough to show off?

154
00:08:21,280 --> 00:08:22,400
Bull's-eye.

155
00:08:26,480 --> 00:08:28,020
What the hell are you doing!
All of a sudden!

156
00:08:28,140 --> 00:08:32,580
Stop asking trivial questions
and focus on my protest!

157
00:08:34,880 --> 00:08:37,000
Weren't you saying violence isn't allowed!

158
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:40,400
How sad! Here, I'm the rule!

159
00:08:42,320 --> 00:08:43,060
Achoo!

160
00:08:47,880 --> 00:08:52,240
This is the winning debate technique!
Here, I'm the rule, see!

161
00:08:52,460 --> 00:08:55,860
That's not debate!
If that's how you want it,

162
00:08:56,320 --> 00:08:57,980
it's the Yōryū-style brawling technique!

163
00:08:58,840 --> 00:09:01,040
You there,
what do you think you're doing to a teacher!

164
00:09:01,300 --> 00:09:03,540
Get over here, teacher!
Senbei, you too, walk over here!

165
00:09:04,280 --> 00:09:06,100
Chen! Chonnyan! Chen!

166
00:09:11,540 --> 00:09:13,920
You seem a little quick-tempered.

167
00:09:13,920 --> 00:09:16,780
You're the one with the far shorter temper!

168
00:09:17,680 --> 00:09:20,640
Earlier, it was to test how patient you are.

169
00:09:20,640 --> 00:09:23,080
I deliberately acted rough.

170
00:09:23,080 --> 00:09:24,040
Seriously?

171
00:09:24,720 --> 00:09:27,260
Being quick-tempered is
caused by a calcium deficiency.

172
00:09:28,480 --> 00:09:30,620
So, whenever you feel like getting angry,

173
00:09:35,580 --> 00:09:37,520
this is Ryotsu's winning debate technique!

174
00:09:37,520 --> 00:09:41,060
take in some calcium the
moment you feel angry, okay?

175
00:09:41,660 --> 00:09:45,580
But taking it in the middle of a debate won't work right away,
you know.

176
00:09:46,620 --> 00:09:48,960
Just do as you're told.

177
00:09:52,400 --> 00:09:54,700
Here, I am the rule.

178
00:09:55,400 --> 00:09:58,140
Your calcium isn't working at all, is it?

179
00:09:59,560 --> 00:10:01,680
That anger just now was an
act I put on deliberately.

180
00:10:01,680 --> 00:10:03,240
I was totally serious, you know!

181
00:10:04,440 --> 00:10:05,160
Listen carefully.

182
00:10:05,700 --> 00:10:09,960
Whether you get through this school safely depends on me,
you know.

183
00:10:09,960 --> 00:10:11,880
You do understand that, don't you?

184
00:10:11,880 --> 00:10:13,280
R-right, I remember.

185
00:10:13,280 --> 00:10:15,920
My bonus is riding on this, isn't it?

186
00:10:16,340 --> 00:10:19,220
I've prepared a wonderful
gift for someone like you.

187
00:10:19,660 --> 00:10:23,160
From the right: premium calcium,
250,000 yen per bottle.

188
00:10:23,780 --> 00:10:26,800
Next to it: somewhat premium calcium,
120,000 yen.

189
00:10:28,140 --> 00:10:29,800
Buy them? You're charging money for this?

190
00:10:30,640 --> 00:10:33,320
Do you want to fix your irritable,
short-tempered lifestyle?

191
00:10:35,300 --> 00:10:36,860
You fix yours first.

192
00:10:36,860 --> 00:10:39,340
Besides,
I don't have the money to buy that stuff.

193
00:10:40,880 --> 00:10:41,560
Then

194
00:10:41,560 --> 00:10:44,620
from today, all your meals will be this.

195
00:10:45,360 --> 00:10:45,720
What?

196
00:10:46,520 --> 00:10:49,200
Small fish that are full of calcium

197
00:10:49,600 --> 00:10:51,520
are the Kaitteru Rebate Jis
(cheap calcium rebate deal).

198
00:10:51,920 --> 00:10:55,140
Because small fish are packed with calcium,

199
00:10:55,140 --> 00:10:57,160
you should make a habit
of eating them every day.

200
00:10:58,480 --> 00:11:01,320
Why do I have to eat nothing but that stuff?

201
00:11:02,160 --> 00:11:04,080
Don't you want your bonus?

202
00:11:04,980 --> 00:11:05,700
That's right.

203
00:11:05,700 --> 00:11:08,700
Fine, fine, I'll eat it, all right?

204
00:11:09,440 --> 00:11:11,420
Then I'm off on patrol, Senior.

205
00:11:16,840 --> 00:11:19,980
Damn it, three days of only small
fish and I'm getting frustrated.

206
00:11:19,980 --> 00:11:21,600
Now I'm even more irritated!

207
00:11:22,120 --> 00:11:24,200
I'll listen to the radio
and calm myself down.

208
00:11:25,120 --> 00:11:27,200
Right, it's about time
for the race to start.

209
00:11:30,180 --> 00:11:31,920
This time, the star is a tanuki.

210
00:11:32,560 --> 00:11:34,980
I'll take this tanuki to
the front of the police box

211
00:11:34,980 --> 00:11:36,040
and sing this:

212
00:11:36,620 --> 00:11:40,680
Tan-tan Tanuki, Officer Tanuki

213
00:11:40,680 --> 00:11:42,780
Comaneci and Rianov!

214
00:11:43,360 --> 00:11:44,620
And finally, the butt.

215
00:11:44,620 --> 00:11:46,120
Pan-pan!

216
00:11:46,120 --> 00:11:46,920
That's fine.

217
00:11:46,920 --> 00:11:47,800
Easy, right?

218
00:11:47,800 --> 00:11:50,700
But won't the police
officer get angry at you?

219
00:11:51,280 --> 00:11:51,640
Don't worry.

220
00:11:52,420 --> 00:11:54,680
If they see this sign,
they'll definitely forgive you.

221
00:11:54,680 --> 00:11:56,440
Because it's famous on TV.

222
00:11:58,140 --> 00:12:01,540
But the hippo carrying a bag
to the bag shop was a huge hit!

223
00:12:02,120 --> 00:12:04,760
If this one turns out well,
I'll consider making you a regular.

224
00:12:05,280 --> 00:12:05,960
Really?

225
00:12:06,240 --> 00:12:07,500
Yes, I'll do my best!

226
00:12:08,960 --> 00:12:09,472
Alright,

227
00:12:09,522 --> 00:12:13,180
That's it, keep it up!
There, right there! Go, go, go, go, go!

228
00:12:14,040 --> 00:12:17,040
Aaargh! Why won't it reach?! Damn it!

229
00:12:18,540 --> 00:12:18,880
What?!

230
00:12:19,240 --> 00:12:22,460
No, no, I accidentally cut it.

231
00:12:23,360 --> 00:12:25,640
What can I do for you?

232
00:12:25,780 --> 00:12:27,360
Well, you see...

233
00:12:28,620 --> 00:12:36,060
Hunter... Tanuki no Omawari-san,
here, the spring ground Andria's... hup!

234
00:12:36,900 --> 00:12:41,640
Right, right, and then, slap on the butt!

235
00:12:41,640 --> 00:12:49,760
Eeeeh? You, Name-san, no,
that's absolutely not the kind of job it is!

236
00:12:49,760 --> 00:12:54,300
It is! Is there really such a ridiculous job?
It's true!

237
00:12:54,300 --> 00:13:00,660
Oh, it's a prank camera!
That prank camera -

238
00:13:00,660 --> 00:13:05,780
So what? If you normally say
"prank camera," people just laugh.

239
00:13:05,780 --> 00:13:09,160
and forgive you, right?
No, no matter how patient I am...

240
00:13:09,160 --> 00:13:13,180
But that just now made me angry!
You're not patient at all!

241
00:13:13,180 --> 00:13:18,400
You, wait right there!
This is going to take a while

242
00:13:20,780 --> 00:13:23,580
Debate also requires a wealth of knowledge.

243
00:13:23,580 --> 00:13:27,580
Ryotsu-kun,
say the full name of Japan's Prime Minister.

244
00:13:28,780 --> 00:13:31,900
Let me see, I think it's Ichiro Yamada.

245
00:13:32,360 --> 00:13:35,140
You idiot, is that how a debate works?

246
00:13:35,140 --> 00:13:39,560
Trying to provoke me won't work.

247
00:13:40,760 --> 00:13:41,760
You've gotten better.

248
00:13:42,100 --> 00:13:45,280
Sure, maybe I can't name
the Prime Minister of Japan.

249
00:13:45,280 --> 00:13:48,460
But I can name every single Digimon.

250
00:13:49,760 --> 00:13:51,140
What good is knowing that?

251
00:13:51,360 --> 00:13:52,755
I'm also well-versed in military weapons,

252
00:13:52,805 --> 00:13:55,960
and I know the proper way
to fire a Patriot missile.

253
00:13:56,380 --> 00:13:59,360
Even knowing that, you still can't hold
a conversation with ordinary people.

254
00:13:59,700 --> 00:14:00,591
How naive.

255
00:14:00,641 --> 00:14:04,720
The people I debate are mostly criminals.

256
00:14:05,800 --> 00:14:09,600
Criminals are people who have
strayed far beyond common sense.

257
00:14:09,820 --> 00:14:13,420
Of course common sense won't
work on people like that.

258
00:14:15,080 --> 00:14:15,820
Well, that's true.

259
00:14:20,760 --> 00:14:21,280
It's a summer one!

260
00:14:21,660 --> 00:14:22,060
I see.

261
00:14:22,720 --> 00:14:25,560
Damn! I got talked into that!

262
00:14:25,820 --> 00:14:26,520
Cut!

263
00:14:27,180 --> 00:14:30,000
So my teaching method
really was good after all.

264
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:32,860
You've mastered debate techniques this well.

265
00:14:32,860 --> 00:14:34,340
So does that mean I'm graduating?

266
00:14:35,280 --> 00:14:36,340
Yes, but

267
00:14:37,140 --> 00:14:37,880
But?

268
00:14:39,060 --> 00:14:39,580
I see.

269
00:14:39,630 --> 00:14:45,340
So if I don't get angry for one day,
I get my diploma?

270
00:14:45,440 --> 00:14:47,600
Yes, and the bonus will be mine too.

271
00:14:48,560 --> 00:14:52,740
I'm sorry, I never imagined it
would be left somewhere like this.

272
00:14:53,440 --> 00:14:58,260
This is the super-rare model kit that the
senior officer imported from overseas, right?

273
00:15:02,600 --> 00:15:07,580
Things with form break someday.
Don't worry about it, Reiko.

274
00:15:08,160 --> 00:15:09,720
I'm really sorry.

275
00:15:09,720 --> 00:15:11,500
It's fine, it's fine.

276
00:15:11,500 --> 00:15:14,440
Sorry, the ball is...

277
00:15:19,020 --> 00:15:21,380
Is this the ball you're looking for?

278
00:15:23,180 --> 00:15:26,280
Don't play in a place like
this from now on, okay?

279
00:15:27,240 --> 00:15:28,040
Yeah, thanks.

280
00:15:29,100 --> 00:15:30,560
You held it together, didn't you?

281
00:15:31,140 --> 00:15:34,260
Back when you were Ryo-chan,
you'd have definitely yelled at them.

282
00:15:34,260 --> 00:15:37,260
Getting angry over something
like this and blowing your bonus,

283
00:15:37,260 --> 00:15:38,620
I'm not that foolish.

284
00:15:38,620 --> 00:15:41,120
From now on,
they'll be calling you Buddha Ryo-san.

285
00:15:41,120 --> 00:15:41,600
Trouble!

286
00:15:42,420 --> 00:15:44,540
A drunk is causing a ruckus over there.

287
00:15:45,760 --> 00:15:46,960
What did you say?

288
00:15:48,420 --> 00:15:49,860
I'm going to drink more!

289
00:15:49,860 --> 00:15:51,260
Come on, this way.

290
00:15:51,260 --> 00:15:53,620
Is Ryo-chan really going to interrogate him?

291
00:15:53,620 --> 00:15:56,600
Leave it to Buddha Ryo-san.

292
00:15:58,420 --> 00:15:59,260
Damn it!

293
00:15:59,260 --> 00:16:01,160
Don't you have any sake? Sake!

294
00:16:01,160 --> 00:16:04,420
Now then, could you tell me your name?

295
00:16:04,420 --> 00:16:06,020
You're an idiot, aren't you?

296
00:16:06,020 --> 00:16:06,940
Desu.

297
00:16:08,600 --> 00:16:10,040
Just kidding, desu!

298
00:16:11,980 --> 00:16:15,600
Senpai, it's important to listen
to what the other person has to say.

299
00:16:15,600 --> 00:16:18,680
I know, don't worry, Nakagawa.

300
00:16:19,180 --> 00:16:20,280
Hey, sake.

301
00:16:20,280 --> 00:16:23,920
You like sake too?
I'm a big sake lover myself.

302
00:16:24,700 --> 00:16:26,720
We get along well, officer.

303
00:16:27,680 --> 00:16:29,242
Sake is delicious, isn't it?

304
00:16:29,292 --> 00:16:31,800
We should drink together properly sometime,
just the two of us.

305
00:16:32,480 --> 00:16:34,620
Right, could you tell me your name?

306
00:16:34,620 --> 00:16:37,520
The name, good, it's written down.

307
00:16:38,020 --> 00:16:38,820
Senpai.

308
00:16:38,820 --> 00:16:40,400
You did it, Ryo-chan.

309
00:16:41,600 --> 00:16:43,100
We're almost there now.

310
00:16:43,100 --> 00:16:44,900
Yes, I wrote it down.

311
00:16:44,900 --> 00:16:45,940
Let's see, let's see.

312
00:16:48,980 --> 00:16:50,500
It's an unusual name, isn't it?

313
00:16:53,200 --> 00:16:55,320
Maybe I should take a little deep breath.

314
00:16:55,320 --> 00:16:58,800
Just kidding, Baketerii.

315
00:17:02,340 --> 00:17:03,220
Senpai

316
00:17:03,220 --> 00:17:04,260
Ryo-chan

317
00:17:07,660 --> 00:17:08,920
He's smiling.

318
00:17:09,980 --> 00:17:10,860
Are you all right?

319
00:17:11,600 --> 00:17:13,160
It's nothing, really. Just this much.

320
00:17:13,160 --> 00:17:16,260
But normally you'd have hit someone long ago,
wouldn't you?

321
00:17:16,260 --> 00:17:18,400
I've been reborn.

322
00:17:18,400 --> 00:17:20,620
Hitting someone during a talk?

323
00:17:20,620 --> 00:17:24,160
There's no way I'd do something like that,
like some old geezer from the old town.

324
00:17:24,840 --> 00:17:26,920
I guess it's the effect of the calcium.

325
00:17:26,920 --> 00:17:28,380
I wonder how long this will last.

326
00:17:28,380 --> 00:17:31,040
Well then, now that the fun's over,

327
00:17:31,040 --> 00:17:33,180
could you tell me your address and name?

328
00:17:34,600 --> 00:17:35,320
Well, let's see.

329
00:17:36,100 --> 00:17:38,280
I'll tell you if you show me your handcuffs.

330
00:17:39,300 --> 00:17:40,160
Nakagawa.

331
00:17:40,160 --> 00:17:40,420
Yes.

332
00:17:40,420 --> 00:17:42,480
Bring me some small fish.

333
00:17:42,480 --> 00:17:44,140
Here you go.

334
00:17:44,140 --> 00:17:46,800
I'd better top up on a little calcium.

335
00:17:47,560 --> 00:17:48,360
Why?

336
00:17:48,360 --> 00:17:50,500
Eating small fish like that...

337
00:17:50,500 --> 00:17:53,320
You're a big eater, you!

338
00:17:56,320 --> 00:18:00,100
Well, actually,
it seems my teacher was a whale.

339
00:18:01,800 --> 00:18:03,300
That laugh is scary.

340
00:18:03,300 --> 00:18:03,780
Really?

341
00:18:04,580 --> 00:18:07,140
Show him the handcuffs,
and he'll definitely talk.

342
00:18:08,860 --> 00:18:09,680
See?

343
00:18:10,440 --> 00:18:12,660
Wow, they're the real thing.

344
00:18:12,660 --> 00:18:15,640
Now, will you tell us?

345
00:18:15,640 --> 00:18:19,000
Officer, you really are a good person.

346
00:18:19,520 --> 00:18:21,940
So will you talk, then?

347
00:18:21,940 --> 00:18:24,220
Yes, I'll tell you anything.

348
00:18:24,220 --> 00:18:26,260
We've finally understood each other!

349
00:18:26,260 --> 00:18:27,940
Senpai, we did it!

350
00:18:27,940 --> 00:18:29,500
Good for you, Ryo-chan.

351
00:18:29,500 --> 00:18:32,280
Well, with Buddha Ryo-san on the job,
what else would you expect?

352
00:18:36,380 --> 00:18:37,740
Fooled you, didn't I?

353
00:18:39,720 --> 00:18:41,740
Officer, you've been caught!

354
00:18:41,740 --> 00:18:43,480
Yes, we did it!

355
00:18:45,300 --> 00:18:46,340
Senpai.

356
00:18:47,960 --> 00:18:50,360
I'm not that easily
Translation>
riled up.

357
00:18:51,620 --> 00:18:53,940
I'm not angry at all, you know.

358
00:18:55,800 --> 00:18:59,180
Isn't that enough playing around?

359
00:19:01,400 --> 00:19:03,200
Now, would you please go home?

360
00:19:04,920 --> 00:19:07,240
I'll write it, I'll write it,
anything you want!

361
00:19:08,280 --> 00:19:08,660
Forgive me!

362
00:19:09,540 --> 00:19:10,500
I... I held out!

363
00:19:10,680 --> 00:19:14,660
But Ryo-chan right now is a
hundred times scarier than usual!

364
00:19:16,400 --> 00:19:18,000
Yes! Yes!

365
00:19:20,220 --> 00:19:21,520
It's big!

366
00:19:22,320 --> 00:19:23,060
Boom!

367
00:19:24,540 --> 00:19:27,980
Once security for this festival is over,
today's work is done, right?

368
00:19:28,540 --> 00:19:30,931
With this, my training is finished.

369
00:19:30,981 --> 00:19:32,860
And I get my bonus...

370
00:19:32,860 --> 00:19:34,200
It's you!

371
00:19:34,800 --> 00:19:38,020
It's not you, it's Katsuda.

372
00:19:39,440 --> 00:19:42,540
Come on, that's rude to Ryotsu-sensei.

373
00:19:42,540 --> 00:19:48,680
Mr. Katsuda came all the way here
to hand you your diploma personally.

374
00:19:49,360 --> 00:19:50,640
That's right.

375
00:19:50,640 --> 00:19:51,160
Hah!

376
00:19:51,160 --> 00:19:53,180
Acho acho acho acho!

377
00:19:53,180 --> 00:19:53,900
Acho!

378
00:20:01,520 --> 00:20:04,200
It'd be better to hand
over the diploma in person,

379
00:20:04,200 --> 00:20:07,760
I'm sure Ryotsu-kun will be
deeply moved and delighted, Ken.

380
00:20:08,240 --> 00:20:10,040
Sensei, sorry for going to all this trouble.

381
00:20:10,040 --> 00:20:12,700
Then you should have gone out earlier.

382
00:20:12,700 --> 00:20:15,760
I can't give you this
until after twelve o'clock.

383
00:20:15,760 --> 00:20:18,500
I'm fine now, honestly.

384
00:20:18,500 --> 00:20:22,220
Nakagawa, is Ryotsu really all right?

385
00:20:23,900 --> 00:20:27,980
No matter what happens, he won't lose his temper.
Well then, we're off on patrol.

386
00:20:32,220 --> 00:20:33,500
Sorry.

387
00:20:34,180 --> 00:20:37,580
It's all right.
There are lots of people out today.

388
00:20:37,580 --> 00:20:39,540
If you run around, you'll get hurt.

389
00:20:39,960 --> 00:20:41,100
Yes, Officer.

390
00:20:41,780 --> 00:20:43,120
Be careful.

391
00:20:43,120 --> 00:20:43,900
Okay~

392
00:20:44,420 --> 00:20:47,280
He really does seem to have
changed his personality.

393
00:20:47,280 --> 00:20:49,880
If he's like this, he seems fine.

394
00:20:49,880 --> 00:20:52,520
Thanks for your hard work, everyone.
Please, help yourselves.

395
00:20:52,970 --> 00:20:55,380
No, we're still on duty.

396
00:20:56,040 --> 00:20:57,140
Sensei, please, have one.

397
00:20:57,980 --> 00:20:59,280
I'm not really one for sake,

398
00:20:59,800 --> 00:21:01,720
but surely one little drink is fine,
isn't it?

399
00:21:01,720 --> 00:21:03,560
After all, it's a festival.

400
00:21:03,560 --> 00:21:04,620
Well, go on.

401
00:21:04,620 --> 00:21:05,740
Don't hold back.

402
00:21:06,640 --> 00:21:07,360
Is that so?

403
00:21:07,740 --> 00:21:08,920
Well then, just one cup.

404
00:21:10,380 --> 00:21:12,280
What a magnificent drinking style!

405
00:21:12,280 --> 00:21:13,620
Impressive indeed.

406
00:21:14,340 --> 00:21:16,300
Looks like today will
also end without incident.

407
00:21:16,880 --> 00:21:17,240
What?

408
00:21:23,520 --> 00:21:24,800
What's going on here?

409
00:21:30,360 --> 00:21:32,980
Do you think I'd drink if
I were scared of the police?

410
00:21:35,200 --> 00:21:36,800
Senpai, that guy...

411
00:21:37,560 --> 00:21:40,200
He's acting up on purpose again to test me,
isn't he?

412
00:21:40,200 --> 00:21:42,040
Leave this to me.

413
00:21:42,540 --> 00:21:44,040
What happened, sensei?

414
00:21:44,760 --> 00:21:46,200
Hey, I've seen that face somewhere.

415
00:21:46,200 --> 00:21:47,320
Playing dumb again

416
00:21:47,320 --> 00:21:49,480
Come on, we're in the way of other people.

417
00:21:49,480 --> 00:21:50,900
Let's go over there.

418
00:21:51,500 --> 00:21:52,720
Don't touch me!

419
00:21:56,540 --> 00:21:57,660
Are you all right, sensei?

420
00:22:00,920 --> 00:22:02,640
Don't stop!

421
00:22:03,360 --> 00:22:07,160
Patience, patience, patience here.

422
00:22:07,900 --> 00:22:10,360
Patience, patience.

423
00:22:11,640 --> 00:22:14,180
He's just drunk and making a scene.

424
00:22:14,740 --> 00:22:17,660
I didn't realize he was such a bad drunk.

425
00:22:17,660 --> 00:22:19,940
So you weren't trying to test your senpai?

426
00:22:19,940 --> 00:22:22,400
You didn't even think about it for a second,
did you?

427
00:22:23,720 --> 00:22:25,300
Is that right?

428
00:22:29,340 --> 00:22:30,900
It's for the bonus.

429
00:22:30,900 --> 00:22:31,920
Patience.

430
00:22:31,920 --> 00:22:34,320
Look, they're about to clash!

431
00:22:34,320 --> 00:22:35,280
Me, I...

432
00:22:35,280 --> 00:22:36,500
Patience.

433
00:22:39,340 --> 00:22:40,620
Can I do it?

434
00:22:40,620 --> 00:22:43,340
Forget the bonus now!

435
00:22:43,340 --> 00:22:44,300
I'm going to knock him flat!

436
00:22:45,340 --> 00:22:46,500
Not yet, not yet.

437
00:22:46,500 --> 00:22:46,940
Here it goes!

438
00:22:52,360 --> 00:22:54,800
The thing I feared most
has finally happened.

439
00:22:55,300 --> 00:22:55,860
Don't say I didn't warn you.

440
00:22:56,280 --> 00:22:57,360
Stop it, not here!

441
00:22:57,660 --> 00:23:00,520
I love liquor, but I hate drunks!

442
00:23:02,120 --> 00:23:04,820
Here I come! I'm unleashing my anger!

443
00:23:05,200 --> 00:23:08,040
Wait! If we talk,
we can surely understand each other!

444
00:23:08,460 --> 00:23:09,660
Shut up!

445
00:23:10,860 --> 00:23:12,300
Stop it, please!

446
00:23:19,460 --> 00:23:20,560
Before you!

447
00:23:20,720 --> 00:23:21,800
Can you forgive that?!

448
00:23:21,860 --> 00:23:22,620
Stop it!

449
00:23:22,620 --> 00:23:23,240
Air sando!

450
00:23:25,780 --> 00:23:27,740
I had a bad feeling about this.

451
00:23:28,340 --> 00:23:31,420
Ryo-chan's personality couldn't change all of a sudden,
could it?

452
00:23:32,440 --> 00:23:34,100
So where is the senior officer now?

453
00:23:34,340 --> 00:23:37,005
So as not to bother the people around him,

454
00:23:37,055 --> 00:23:39,940
he's continuing his special training,
just the two of them.

455
00:23:40,460 --> 00:23:43,480
Hey, that's dirty!
It's the fish we caught together!

456
00:23:43,920 --> 00:23:47,060
Fish bones are packed with calcium,
you know.

457
00:23:47,300 --> 00:23:49,040
I'll give you the bones later, I promise!

458
00:23:49,280 --> 00:23:52,180
What the hell are you saying?!
Give me some too! Take this!

459
00:23:52,620 --> 00:23:53,520
This is bad!

460
00:23:53,560 --> 00:23:54,200
Stop it!

461
00:23:54,320 --> 00:23:55,400
Stop it, I said stop!

462
00:24:24,100 --> 00:24:25,500
Thank you for watching.

